        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIt is not in dispute that the applicant is a juvenile and is entitled to the benefits of the provisions of the Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0dca4601860741eab0d2aacd2c41f620_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Under Section 12 of the Act, the prayer for bail of a juvenile may be rejected 'if there appear reasonable grounds for believing that the release of the juvenile is likely to bring him into association with any known criminal or expose him "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "75eb42a2685542c085770036f44a9d7b_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThe court has to see whether the opinion of the learned appellate Court as well as Juvenile Justice Board recorded in the impugned judgment and orders are in consonance with the provision of the Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "42b5607f32334c1fac2c8995a915e3b3_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Section 12 of the Act lays down three contingencies in which bail may be refused to a juvenile offender."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "527a877253a148a5ba00ea0f729a70b8_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "These are:-\n(i) if the release is likely to bring him into association with any known criminal, or (ii) expose him to moral, physical or psychological danger, or (iii) that his release would defeat the ends of justice?"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "369200848cb34a6492becf49319861c4_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nGravity of the offence has not been mentioned as a ground to reject the bail."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1e812ca2997a45fc98bc19daa0075026_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is not a relevant factor while considering to grant bail to the juvenile."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bb10ba55e00a4836a63956d879360ea6_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It has been so held by this Court in Shiv Kumar alias Sadhu Vs. State of U.P. 2010 (68) ACC 616(LB)."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "beebdf769359445d9729664c4a442af7_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It has been consistently followed in subsequent decisions of this court."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "19e8471e86c94305bfde6aa2e2451c7a_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThus, it remains largely undisputed that the applicant - was a juvenile on the date of occurrence;\ndoes not appear to be prone to criminal proclivity or criminal psychology, in light of the observations of the D.P.O; does not have a crimin"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d64453c6cc3a4a04a2dcebdb94bda0cf_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Even otherwise, there does not appear to exist any factor or circumstance mentioned in section 12 of the Act as may dis-entitle the applicant to grant of bail, at this stage."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "21ca1f3c7d6e4875a87b10b8b1f0e364_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The father of the applicant undertakes to address the statutory concerns expressed in section 12 of the Act, as to the safety and well being of the applicant, upon his release."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5d9f6fcdb37049fcbbc63163b5ce5d7a_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIn view of the above, it appears that the findings recorded by the learned Court below are in conflict with the settled principle in law, for the purpose of grant of bail and are erroneous and contrary to the law laid down by this court."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e5f88c276c4342e4ba25eb64309c0bd8_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Consequently, those orders cannot be sustained."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cf696abc08af46a48ac4bb948f34daec_60",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
            "matched_text": "set aside",
            "start": 41,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "The aforesaid impugned orders are hereby set aside."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c413082acfee46258627dcf43f8407b8_61",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nIn view of the observations made above, the present criminal revision is allowed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "aafb5d5a178942eea69598b07a5699e5_62",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Let the applicant,\nJuvenile X, involved in the aforesaid case crime be released on bail, on his furnishing personal bond with two sureties each of like amount, to the satisfaction of the court concerned with the following conditions:\nJuveni"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "972490abe5cf410dab69bde1e6a8a972_63",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "(i) The applicant shall not tamper with the evidence or threaten the witnesses;"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b16f02b296fa4c51b616ca73296215cc_64",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(ii) The applicant through guardian shall file an undertaking to the effect that he shall not seek any adjournment on the date fixed for evidence when the witnesses are present in court."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b555a92e27984aafa7928cc543a721e1_65",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In case of default of this condition, it shall be open for the trial Court to treat it as abuse of liberty of bail and pass orders in accordance with law;"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9304afcf9c804da193f8772e7d259307_66",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(iii) The applicant through guardian shall remain present before the trial Court on each date fixed, either personally or through his counsel."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "91abc773763943cbb825a9605b79fc18_67",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In case of his absence,\nwithout sufficient cause, the trial Court may proceed against him under Section 229-A of the Indian Penal Code."
      }
    ],
